The de Broglie wavelength formula is:

\[
\lambda = \frac{h}{p}
\]

where \( p = mv \) is the momentum of the particle.

---

**(a) Truck:**
- Mass \( m = 10,000 \, \text{kg} \)
- Velocity \( v = 27.8 \, \text{m/s} \)
- Momentum \( p = 10,000 \times 27.8 = 278,000 \, \text{kg·m/s} \)
- Wavelength \( \lambda = \frac{6.626 \times 10^{-34}}{278,000} \approx 2.38 \times 10^{-37} \, \text{cm} \)

---

**(b) Flea:**
- Mass \( m = 50 \, \text{mg} = 50 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{kg} \)
- Velocity \( v = 1 \, \text{m/s} \)
- Momentum \( p = 50 \times 10^{-6} \times 1 = 50 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{kg·m/s} \)
- Wavelength \( \lambda = \frac{6.626 \times 10^{-34}}{50 \times 10^{-6}} \approx 1.325 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{cm} \)

---

**(c) Water molecule:**
- Mass \( m = 18 \, \text{amu} \approx 18 \times 1.66 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg} \approx 3.0 \times 10^{-26} \, \text{kg} \)
- Velocity \( v = 500 \, \text{m/s} \)
- Momentum \( p = 3.0 \times 10^{-26} \times 500 = 1.5 \times 10^{-23} \, \text{kg·m/s} \)
- Wavelength \( \lambda = \frac{6.626 \times 10^{-34}}{1.5 \times 10^{-23}} \approx 4.417 \times 10^{-10} \, \text{cm} \)

---

Comparing these values with the options, the closest match is:

**E. 2.4 × 10^-37 cm, 1.3 × 10^-27 cm, 4.43 × 10^-10 cm**

