   \]
   For a toroid, the magnetic field \( B \) is uniform along the circular path of radius \( r \), so:
   \[
   B \cdot 2\pi r = \mu_0 N I
   \]
   where \( N = 500 \) turns, \( I = 4 \) A, and \( r = 15 \) cm = 0.15 m.

   Rearranging for \( B \):
   \[
   B = \frac{\mu_0 N I}{2\pi r}
   \]
   Substituting values:
   \[
   B = \frac{(4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{Tm/A}) \times 500 \times 4}{2\pi \times 0.15 \, \text{m}}
   \]
   Simplifying:
   \[
   B = \frac{4\pi \times 10^{-7} \times 500 \times 4}{2\pi \times 0.15} = \frac{8 \times 10^{-4}}{0.3} = 2.67 \times 10^{-3} \, \text{T}
   \]

