We have a normal distribution with mean \(\mu = 3250\) and standard deviation \(\sigma = 320\). For the middle 50% of days, we want the range corresponding to the 25th and 75th percentiles.

1. The z-score for the 25th percentile is approximately \(-0.6745\).
2. The z-score for the 75th percentile is approximately \(0.6745\).

Now, convert these z-scores to the corresponding values in the distribution:
\[
\text{Lower bound} = \mu + z \cdot \sigma = 3250 + (-0.6745) \cdot 320 \approx 3250 - 216.64 = 3033.36
\]
\[
\text{Upper bound} = \mu + z \cdot \sigma = 3250 + 0.6745 \cdot 320 \approx 3250 + 216.64 = 3466.64
\]

Rounding to the nearest whole number, the range is approximately (3034, 3466).

